  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Fortress. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Fortress is a challenging open-information Solitaire (Patience) game characterized by its unique building rules and lack of a draw pile. All cards are dealt at the start; the top card of each column is available. Tableau builds up or down by same suit; empty spaces may be filled with any available card. Goal: move all 52 cards to the four foundations (ace to king by suit).',
    objective: 'Move all 52 cards into the four foundation piles, building each suit up from Ace to King.',
    gameplay: 'Only the top card of each tableau column is available. Move a card to a foundation (build up by suit from ace to king) or to another tableau column (build up or down by same suit, one card at a time; no round-the-corner). Fill an empty tableau space with any available card. No redeal.',
    keyRules: [
      'Only the exposed (top) card of each column is available.',
      'Foundations build up by suit from ace to king.',
      'Tableau builds up or down by same suit; one card at a time.',
      'Aces cannot be placed on kings or vice versa.',
      'Empty spaces may be filled with any available card.',
      'No redeal.',
    ],
